```java
class BankAccount {
    public double balance; // public field: anyone can corrupt it
}

// Every caller must remember the rules — and one forgets:
account.balance = account.balance - 100; // no overdraft check
account.balance = -500;                  // invalid state, no one stopped it
```

```java
class BankAccount {
    private double balance; // hidden state

    public void withdraw(double amount) {
        if (amount <= 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Amount must be positive");
        if (amount > balance) throw new IllegalStateException("Insufficient funds");
        balance -= amount; // validated in ONE place
    }

    public double getBalance() { return balance; } // read-only outside
}

account.withdraw(100); // intent only; rules enforced inside
```
*Switch `balance` from `double` to `BigDecimal` later and not a single caller changes.*

